    "summary": "Scorching Eyes→Stella→Franklin suite & tight second‑set jams",
    "blurb": "The night peaks with a fiery Eyes‑Stella‑Franklin’s Tower sequence and a powerful Lazy Lightning > Supplication in the first set. Jerry delivers transcendent leads on Stella Blue while the band locks into a seamless second‑set flow highlighted by Ship Of Fools and Estimated Prophet. Overall performance is strong, though Keith's overly percussive keyboard tone shows up at times.",
    "review": "On January 30, 1978 at Chicago’s Uptown Theater the Dead turned in one of their early‑’78 high points. The first set builds from solid rockers into a blistering Lazy Lightning > Supplication stretch that showcases Jerry’s searing lead work and Phil’s supportive bass groove. The second set is where the show truly shines: a seamless Eyes‑Stella‑Franklin’s Tower suite rolls into Ship Of Fools, Estimated Prophet, and an inspired run through Eyes Of The World before closing with a heartfelt Stella Blue and a rousing Franklin’s Tower. While Keith Godchaux’s keyboard can sound a bit percussive, the overall mix is clear and the band’s chemistry is evident throughout. Fans looking for the definitive version of this night should start with the Miller‑remastered soundboard capture, which preserves every nuance of that legendary second‑set flow.",
